WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.880
Dr. Crocker selected three unassembled IKEA
STEFAN chairs, as well as two assembly manuals,

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:06.880
for experimentation.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:11.470
First, one unassembled chair was placed inside
on "Fine," without a manual.

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:14.889
The output produced was an assembled chair,
the pieces put together at random.

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:20.080
Next, an unassembled chair was placed on the
same setting, along with its assembly manual.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:24.440
The output produced was an assembled chair,
with the front and back legs swapped, and

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.620
damage to its seat as if someone had hit it
with a hammer in frustration.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:32.870
For the final trial, Dr. Crocker placed an
unassembled chair, a manual, and a note reading

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.170
"You can do it!"

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:36.260
inside, on the setting "Very Fine."

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:42.530
The Clockworks produced not a chair, but a
60cm wooden automaton with an obsessive enthusiasm

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:45.950
for assembling furniture, though it was not
especially good at it.

